      ],
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            339,
            389
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "A custom theme is an override, not a replacement. "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            389,
            407
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "extends: default"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            407,
            723
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " names the\ntheme it starts from and the rest of the map is a patch: the tokens listed here\nwin, every token not listed keeps the value the base gave it, and the marks,\nstatus colours and scheme all come through untouched. A document that wants\none different grey should have to write one line, not restate a palette."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        339,
        723
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            725,
            776
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The palette is the exception to the patching rule. "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            776,
            789
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "categorical"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            789,
            1056
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " is assigned in\nfixed order and never cycled, so a partial list would silently change which\nseries got which colour; it replaces the base's list outright, and with it the\nbase's validation verdict, because a verdict about a palette says nothing about\na different one."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        725,
        1056
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
